<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-19T21:12:12Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Art crime detective Arthur Brand warns: 'All museums have been, and will be, victims of theft'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed49dfe0715b03fe28b861128a031461bd1883c612e92265a64cdfb368833af1</id><updated>2026-10-19T21:11:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T20:16:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261019-art-crime-detective-arthur-brand-warns-all-museums-have-been-and-will-be-victims-of-theft--d60c97e725cd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261019-art-crime-detective-arthur-brand-warns-all-museums-have-been-and-will-be-victims-of-theft" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome art crime detective Arthur Brand. "In the old days they stole a painting, but a painting is unique; you cannot cut it in two," explains Brand, "In the last 10 years they have been targeting more and more objects made of gold, silver". He examines the transformation of international art theft, warning that increasingly sophisticated criminal opportunism is shifting attention from irreplaceable paintings towards precious metals and gemstones that can be dismantled, melted down or dispersed.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>France riots: AI photos falsely depict elderly couple ‘stripped and robbed’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c31c116b19702d5a1c97746d932a9f3cc59022fdd2cef09717bfc41830ca5d2</id><updated>2026-10-19T21:11:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T20:06:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-riots-ai-photos-falsely-depict-elderly-couple-stripped-and-robbed-1--297fdf860b3d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-riots-ai-photos-falsely-depict-elderly-couple-stripped-and-robbed-1" /><summary type="html">AI-generated photos falsely claiming to show an elderly couple being “stripped and robbed” during unrest in France have racked up millions of views. Amplified by far-right accounts, the images fuelled inflammatory claims about Muslims, Jews and the riots. The FRANCE 24 Observers traced one image to an AI photo montage published by a pro-Israel account. The images were created using OpenAI tools, and the alleged assault remains unverified, with no official reports confirming the attack.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>France faces reckoning with public order policing after violent protest weekend</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:30456ae9cb2781b06b4fd66fd3dba1d03c196956e87b59cd63066df0079cd82b</id><updated>2026-10-19T21:11:09Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T19:56:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261019-france-faces-reckoning-public-order-policing-after-violent-protest-weekend--7b15274e5acb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261019-france-faces-reckoning-public-order-policing-after-violent-protest-weekend" /><summary type="html">France reeled Monday after a weekend of nationwide unrest sparked by mass protests against the rising cost of living and in support of high school students’ demands over education funding. In the violent clashes that erupted, law enforcement officers and protesters were wounded, public buildings were set ablaze and businesses were looted, raising significant questions about the French police's approach to public order.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>French far right seeks to capitalise on protests with calls for law and order</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:933cba94d796edd05d334a2ac30212588595dbcbf5f70d2099f892407c41d0aa</id><updated>2026-10-19T21:11:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T19:41:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/french-far-right-seeks-to-capitalise-on-protests-with-calls-for-law-and-order--1509cdbfc4de.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/french-far-right-seeks-to-capitalise-on-protests-with-calls-for-law-and-order" /><summary type="html">In the wake of the weekend's violence, the political camps have been trading blame for the “chaos”. The riots have played into the hands of the far-right National Rally, which has been quick to capitalise on the anger and fears over law and order. FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell takes a look.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia-China-US summit would prolong the war, Kyiv says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a90b90037f7adaeab7ad1ca784661ff73d5bd6c8e44bbb0f4a19dee8bcbfa670</id><updated>2026-10-19T21:11:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T19:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russia-china-us-summit-would-prolong-the-war-kyiv-says--45dc255a1fdb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-china-us-summit-would-prolong-the-war-kyiv-says" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian ⁠Foreign Minister ​Andrii Sybiha said on ​Monday that a summit between Russia, China ​and the ‌US would ⁠encourage President Vladimir Putin ‌to prolong the war. The ​Wall Street Journal reported that Putin had proposed a ​summit next month ​with US ​President Donald Trump and Chinese President ​Xi Jinping to negotiate an end to the war on terms ⁠that would favour Moscow. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Paris weekend riots raise concerns for tourism industry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b7fbc8c055a3889c2ee7f08dc5bc3a69741344b89ca4ae7da45b32b9c4b4e34b</id><updated>2026-10-19T21:11:18Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T19:06:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/paris-weekend-riots-raise-concerns-for-tourism-industry--69e9afb402b2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/paris-weekend-riots-raise-concerns-for-tourism-industry" /><summary type="html">France announced partial curfews in Paris and other cities on Monday after weekend demonstrations over soaring prices degenerated into some of the worst street violence in recent years. Images of riots and looting in France over the weekend have been seen across the world and are worrying the country's tourism industry. Could the violence put off foreign tourists from visiting? FRANCE 24's Selina Sykes reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Zelensky says Starshield speed limits slowing down frontline response</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9a1c580ffd49fe234270f4c8077909504f15a1c3f4c9c7952751e2c88347a6ee</id><updated>2026-10-19T21:11:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T18:45:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/zelensky-says-starshield-speed-limits-slowing-down-frontline-response--337310623a55.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/zelensky-says-starshield-speed-limits-slowing-down-frontline-response" /><summary type="html">Speed limits on a US military grade satellite system are hindering Ukrainian forces' ability to coordinate drone strikes against Russian forces, President Volodymyr Zelensky said on Monday. Zelensky said frontline units had reported that the Starshield equipment "stops functioning at speeds of 130-160 kilometres (80-100 miles) per hour in various sectors of the front". Separately, a Ukrainian army brigade has announced the rescue of a wounded soldier from the front line using an aerial drone, describing the evacuation as the first of its kind. The brigade published a video showing the drone lowering itself to the ground, before a man in combat gear fastens himself to a winch onboard and is lifted upwards. FRANCE 24's Gulliver Cragg reports from Ukraine.</summary></entry><entry><title>🔴 France issues curfew for parts of central Paris</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f1166c84d7a18c218b4b901f7c6a958f39d27ccf990ef98071756e9a738ffe45</id><updated>2026-10-19T21:11:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T17:09:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261019-live-french-pm-lecornu-calls-for-partial-curfews-in-cities-hit-by-riots-and-looting--ba039b010c2b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261019-live-french-pm-lecornu-calls-for-partial-curfews-in-cities-hit-by-riots-and-looting" /></entry><entry><title>France: ‘localised’ curfews announced after weekend of violence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a93caed00a4bb756c84b3344e604f4d5e0ae6825bb66cba2b1fa2d07e1092e58</id><updated>2026-10-19T21:11:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T16:44:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-localised-curfews-announced-after-weekend-scenes-of-violence--1012a9d0f2f9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-localised-curfews-announced-after-weekend-scenes-of-violence" /><summary type="html">Following a weekend of #violence and #looting, the French government has announced localised #curfews, financial support for affected businesses and a tougher judicial response, while keeping the option of a state of emergency on the table.</summary></entry><entry><title>DZ Mafia murder trial set to begin near Marseille</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d5f5f3dd4f567d7bafcae69dec9dc5db2fcf72eecb04c89096d5cb737cb8ee59</id><updated>2026-10-19T21:11:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T15:58:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261019-dz-mafia-murder-trial-set-to-begin-near-marseille--ec8ee72fba71.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261019-dz-mafia-murder-trial-set-to-begin-near-marseille" /><summary type="html">Five men with alleged connections to the major criminal group DZ Mafia are accused of murdering, in 2020, the elder brother of anti-drug activist Amine Kessaci – now deputy mayor of Aix-en-Provence. The trial, set to begin on Monday, highlights the threat posed by mafia-style drug trafficking networks in the region. FRANCE 24’s Delano D’Souza reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine deploys drone to airlift wounded soldier in 'world-first' operation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ee207fd84e4fbfc0d84b5e5405b991de7dd6f0d64d2badfc7080c4c698da7706</id><updated>2026-10-19T21:11:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T15:44:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261019-ukraine-deploys-drone-airlift-wounded-soldier-world-first-operation--49138a212dd7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261019-ukraine-deploys-drone-airlift-wounded-soldier-world-first-operation" /><summary type="html">Ukraine has evacuated a wounded soldier from the front line using an aerial drone in what a Ukrainian army brigade has described as a world-first operation. The successful mission highlights the growing role of unmanned technology in battlefield evacuations as drones continue to shape the conflict between Ukraine and Russia.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>France wants curfews in some areas after weekend of riots</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e2ba9438c73bf473b9464f79c86573063da30767cf2993668a74c0ff469a3d88</id><updated>2026-10-19T21:11:36Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T15:37:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261019-france-wants-curfews-in-some-areas-after-weekend-of-riots--50625ac5e523.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261019-france-wants-curfews-in-some-areas-after-weekend-of-riots" /><summary type="html">France's central government asked some local authorities to impose curfews and faced pressure over security failings on Monday after a weekend of riots and looting borne out of nationwide anti-government protests. Prime Minister Sébastien Lecornu did not rule out declaring state of emergency but said it was more appropriate for now to apply partial and localised curfews, without providing details of which cities would be affected.</summary></entry><entry><title>France protests: Who are the people arrested during the unrest?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:78f37819bb26c3d7df9ee584e595e4355dce39ba930f665c8466ae40c469a2ac</id><updated>2026-10-19T21:11:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T15:36:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261019-france-protests-who-are-the-people-arrested-during-the-unrest--58595a4cd6f8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261019-france-protests-who-are-the-people-arrested-during-the-unrest" /><summary type="html">At least 2,400 people were arrested in France during protests over the weekend, some simply for being in the wrong place at the wrong time, others on suspicion of theft and looting. In an official address, French President Emmanuel Macron warned that “those who looted will have to pay for the damage”. But who exactly are these rioters?</summary></entry><entry><title>'Police weren't overwhelmed by people protesting and marching' about education and cost of living</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:098d5a1ed010a239d2b473917bffe4c0172d04e638a93bef22aeff093588e6fa</id><updated>2026-10-19T21:11:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T14:58:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261019-police-weren-t-overwhelmed-by-people-protesting-and-marching-about-education-and-cost-of-li--80eee2e21bb0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261019-police-weren-t-overwhelmed-by-people-protesting-and-marching-about-education-and-cost-of-living" /><summary type="html">Oliver Farry is pleased to welcome Andrew Smith, Lecturer in Liberal Arts at Queen Mary University of London. France's escalating social unrest has exposed a troubling disconnect between legitimate popular grievances and the government's increasingly security-focused response. Smith argues that the violence accompanying otherwise largely peaceful demonstrations reveals serious failures of policing, while President Emmanuel Macron's response offers "very little of substance." Drawing parallels with France's historic protest movements, Smith identifies a "convergence of causes" rooted in economic insecurity, educational inequalities and political paralysis. He warns that a repressive response risks deepening the crisis, calling instead for a renewed commitment to "participatory social democracy."</summary></entry><entry><title>Four soldiers dead, dozens injured in fire at Canada military base</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:43bf3b61a18acf06a824abe566de7663cd749f848cb743ed3b22ece17ed7518d</id><updated>2026-10-19T21:11:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T14:25:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261019-four-soldiers-dead-dozens-injured-in-fire-at-canada-military-base--5b7bd85ac81d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261019-four-soldiers-dead-dozens-injured-in-fire-at-canada-military-base" /><summary type="html">Four soldiers were killed and dozens injured in a fire at a military base in Alberta province, one of the worst peacetime tragedies to hit Canada's armed forces on home soil, Prime Minister Mark Carney said Sunday.</summary></entry><entry><title>French PM says 'ultra-left' seeking 'deep unrest' ahead of election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:23d334ae67b1f94c570ea1af289db94ce8d67089844c7f8ffbd545fd853e95f2</id><updated>2026-10-19T21:11:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T14:20:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261019-french-pm-says-ultra-left-seeking-deep-unrest-ahead-of-election--6cf238654fd2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261019-french-pm-says-ultra-left-seeking-deep-unrest-ahead-of-election" /><summary type="html">French Prime Minister Sebastien Lecornu on Monday accused the "ultra-left movement" of seeking to "orchestrate deep unrest across the country" in the runup to next year's presidential election. FRANCE 24 International Affairs Editor Angela Diffley looks back at Lecornu's remarks in the wake of the violent protests that shook the country over the weekend.</summary></entry><entry><title>Brazil court orders Meta to prove it gives Lula, Bolsonaro campaign content equal treatment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8661434997bef40d6875d7245e4b821aa7e3f76fecb983547746a0a00b7c2577</id><updated>2026-10-19T21:11:51Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T14:16:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261019-brazil-court-orders-meta-prove-gives-lula-bolsonaro-campaign-content-equal-treatment--983975c9bef7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261019-brazil-court-orders-meta-prove-gives-lula-bolsonaro-campaign-content-equal-treatment" /><summary type="html">Brazil’s top electoral court has given Meta 24 hours to prove it is treating campaign content from incumbent President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva and Senator Flavio Bolsonaro equally on its online platforms, threatening a daily fine for noncompliance. The ruling follows allegations from Lula's campaign that the social media giant is suppressing Lula’s campaign content ahead of Sunday’s closely contested presidential runoff.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>France protests draw global attention: Trump, Vance blame immigration for unrest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:077907b144d8223f6ff63905aa275f231a53c6d33312faaa8c5e133e0f2f5a55</id><updated>2026-10-19T21:11:54Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T14:04:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261019-france-protests-draw-global-attention-trump-vance-blame-immigration-for-unrest--93b1e8eeacc1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261019-france-protests-draw-global-attention-trump-vance-blame-immigration-for-unrest" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Sunday blamed immigration for unrest during protests in France and urged the country to tighten its migration rules. Trump's post comes after similar comments made by Vice President JD Vance on Saturday. Vance, who is seen as a potential presidential candidate in the 2028 election, also drew a connection to upcoming midterm races for congressional seats on November 3, where Republicans are not expected to perform well. FRANCE 24's Fraser Jackson reports from the United States.</summary></entry><entry><title>Macron kicks off three-day Gulf tour, seeks securing fuel supplies amid crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dffca06d76721a4de6695903ce17eb52156e995279fa4d9322a13c1d1f05ae75</id><updated>2026-10-19T21:11:57Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T14:02:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261019-macron-kicks-off-three-day-gulf-tour-seeks-securing-fuel-supplies-amid-crisis--643ebeff66e0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261019-macron-kicks-off-three-day-gulf-tour-seeks-securing-fuel-supplies-amid-crisis" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron on Monday began a Gulf tour aimed at securing oil and diesel supplies in an effort to bring down prices, after a weekend of violent protests sparked by soaring living costs. Macron, just hours after slamming France's "unbridled" violence in an address late on Sunday, arrived in OPEC member Kuwait where he was welcomed by the emir, Sheikh Mishal Al-Ahmad Al-Jaber Al-Sabah. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Kethevane Gorjestani tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Drone attacks kill scores in Sudan's West Kordofan state and capital Khartoum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b51ea4b42bdde04ef6c86434c2e01516a277092a4ac2489a5360be44111d1273</id><updated>2026-10-19T21:12:00Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T14:00:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261019-drone-attack-near-southern-sudan-market-kills-scores--3bb8acb831d9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261019-drone-attack-near-southern-sudan-market-kills-scores" /><summary type="html">At least 80 people were killed in a drone strike near a market in Sudan’s southern West Kordofan state, a medical source and a witness said Monday, in one of the deadliest single attacks since the Sudan war erupted in 2023. A separate drone attack Monday in the capital Khartoum killed four, including three children.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>US midterms elections: Why data centers are becoming a key issue</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:224d872aab51a95a4f66f5bb740f9ce30c8477c6489c905ea5266ff4b4883c2f</id><updated>2026-10-19T21:12:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T13:59:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261019-us-midterms-elections-why-data-centers-are-becoming-a-key-issue--158f3562e0e4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261019-us-midterms-elections-why-data-centers-are-becoming-a-key-issue" /><summary type="html">With the US midterm elections just weeks away, data centers are emerging as a major political issue for both Republicans and Democrats. There are about 3,000 facilities currently operating in the country. With that number potentially doubling in the coming years, concern – and, in some cases, anger – is growing among voters. FRANCE 24's Fraser Jackson report from West Virginia.</summary></entry><entry><title>France: Police and protesters clash violently over the weekend</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:386261f6db90d9a039266b72e5570aefb96b6d52765e0a922e734fce2eb53131</id><updated>2026-10-19T21:12:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T13:25:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261019-france-police-and-protesters-clash-violently-over-the-weekend--8924f2a53280.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261019-france-police-and-protesters-clash-violently-over-the-weekend" /><summary type="html">Hundreds of thousands took to the streets to protest higher living costs and the poor conditions in schools and other public services in France over the weekend. Police arrested nearly 2,400 people after violent groups clashed with officers and looted shops.The widespread unrest deepens political uncertainty in France as it prepares for elections in six months.</summary></entry><entry><title>French PM Lecornu says ready to declare state of emergency 'if needed'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b110259aa3f9691b894f70649f786773a2721d9b93bb44ad11b862840f3ec19e</id><updated>2026-10-19T21:12:09Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T12:51:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261019-french-pm-says-could-declare-state-of-emergency-over-unrest-if-needed--b945a8529973.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261019-french-pm-says-could-declare-state-of-emergency-over-unrest-if-needed" /><summary type="html">French Prime Minister Sébastien Lecornu on Monday warned that he was prepared to declare a state of emergency as authorities struggled to contain ongoing violence after looting affected thousands of businesses over the weekend. The unrest linked to a student protest movement comes months before France’s presidential election, raising concerns over public security and political stability.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>France 'has to assist' Gulf states, diplomat says as Macron makes three-day visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d844c76df04cd056c1457efc5fe6a7569ca4f0d689966393f2516577b442dee6</id><updated>2026-10-19T21:12:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T12:43:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261019-france-has-to-assist-gulf-states-diplomat-says-as-macron-makes-three-day-visit--6a87f317e16d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261019-france-has-to-assist-gulf-states-diplomat-says-as-macron-makes-three-day-visit" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron is making a three-day visit to the Gulf states focused on fuel supplies and strategic ties. The French leader will first visit Kuwait before heading to the United Arab Emirates, Bahrain and Qatar. The Elysée Palace said Macron would seek commitments for additional deliveries of diesel and petrol that could increase supplies available to France.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry></feed>
